{"step_index":83,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-30T05:35:48Z","content":"# 🎓 Student Survival App 🧑‍🎓🔥\n> **Tagline:** *“Survive college. One deadline at a time. 😂”*  \n> **Subtitle:** *“Because college is already hard enough 😭”*  \n> **Made by students, for students ❤️**  \n> *“Now go study... or at least pretend to. 😂”*\n\n---\n\n### 🚀 Recommended Active Workspace\nThe complete application has been built in your project directory:\n👉 **`C:\\Users\\DELL\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\student-survival-app`**  \n*(I recommend setting this directory as your active workspace in Antigravity).*\n\nIt has also been synchronized to your Desktop directory for immediate access:  \n📁 **`C:\\Users\\DELL\\OneDrive\\Desktop\\student survival\\student-survival-app`**\n\nTo launch the app immediately, simply open **[`index.html`](file:///C:/Users/DELL/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/student-survival-app/index.html)** in any web browser (**Google Chrome, Microsoft Edge, Brave, Safari, Firefox**). Zero build steps or npm installations are required!\n\n---\n\n## 🖼️ Visual Identity: “Life of a Student” Artwork\n\nThe uploaded **“Life of a Student”** notebook illustration (depicting the teacher sitting on Mid, Quiz, Project, Assignments, and the crushed student) is the core visual theme:\n\n1. **App Icon & Logo**:\n   - Clean rounded-square crop with glowing borders and glass badge on the splash screen, login page, top header, profile, and browser favicon.\n2. **Full-Screen Background**:\n   - Set with `background-size: cover; background-position: center; background-attachment: fixed;` so the artwork never stretches or distorts.\n   - Intelligently positioned on mobile screens so the notebook title and cartoon remain visible.\n   - Paired with a dark translucent glassmorphism overlay (`backdrop-filter: blur(16px)`) ensuring text readability.\n\n---\n\n## ✨ Features & Architecture Overview\n\n### 1. ⏳ Animated Loading / Splash Screen\n- **Duration**: ~2.5 seconds with live progress bar (`0%` to `100%`) and status messages.\n- **Dynamic Quotes**: Smoothly cycles through funny student thoughts:\n<truncated 4817 bytes>\nnated ⚡**\n- Smart verdicts based on physical exhaustion vs exam proximity:\n  - *“📚 STUDY! Your exam is coming.”*\n  - *“😴 SLEEP! A tired brain learns nothing.”*\n  - *“📝 Finish the assignment first. Then sleep peacefully.”*\n  - *“☕ Coffee + Study + Regret = College Life.”*\n  - *“😭 You opened the app instead of studying. Nice.”*\n- **Built-in 20-Minute Power Nap Timer** with start/pause/reset and an audio wake-up alarm chime.\n\n### 10. 📱 Mobile-First Experience\n- Sleek bottom navigation bar: **🏠 Home**, **📊 Attend**, **📝 Tasks** (with red notification badge), **📅 Schedule**, **⏳ Exams**.\n- Touch targets $\\ge 44\\text{px}$.\n- Intelligently cropped background illustration that remains crisp and visible.\n\n### 11. 💾 LocalStorage & Profile Management\n- Browser `localStorage` maintains student credentials, attendance, assignments, timetable, and exams across browser refreshes.\n- Profile modal to edit name, email, and branch, or reset to sample data anytime.\n- Logout confirmation modal:\n  - *“Are you sure you want to escape Survival Mode? 😂”*\n  - **Stay 😭** | **Logout 🚪**\n\n### 12. 🔊 Web Audio API Sound Synthesizer\n- Built-in zero-dependency sound synthesis for UI taps, celebratory victory chimes, alerts, and alarm bells. Mute/unmute toggle available in the header.\n\n---\n\n## 📂 Project Structure\n\n```\nstudent-survival-app/\n│\n├── index.html                   # Entry point (Tailwind CDN, semantic HTML5, modals)\n├── styles.css                   # Glassmorphism, animations, cover background positioning\n├── app.js                       # State machine, math engine, real-time tickers, audio synthesizer\n├── README.md                    # Documentation & college presentation walkthrough\n│\n└── assets/\n    ├── life-of-a-student.jpg    # Uploaded notebook illustration\n    ├── logo.jpg                 # App logo\n    └── student-life-logo.svg    # Vector artwork\n```\n\nAll files are ready to view, test, and demonstrate!","thinking":"The instruction specifies that a new project requires creating a subdirectory within the default project location, since the user has no active workspace. Therefore, project creation involves establishing this subdirectory. Furthermore, the user should be advised to set this newly created subdirectory as the active workspace.\n\n\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
